  "note": "Split engine. calculateVaccinationStatus(data) returns { level, score, firedRules }: if fewer than 5 of the 19 scored items (14 vaccines 0/1/2, 4 consent Likert 1-5, post-vaccination observation 1-5) are answered it short-circuits to level 'draft', score 0, no rules; otherwise score = round(vaccineScore*0.8 + consentScore*0.2) where vaccineScore = mean(answered vaccines)/2*100 and consentScore = (mean(answered consent)-1)/4*100 (unanswered items are simply excluded, so a sparsely answered form is not penalised), and level = 'contraindicated' if previousAnaphylaxis === 'yes', else upToDate (>=80) / partiallyComplete (>=40) / overdue. firedRules are the 20 VAX-0NN rules in catalogue order (high, then medium, then low 'positive' rules). form-app.js (window.submitForm) calls detectAdditionalFlags(data) separately and stores it as additionalFlags, mirrored by flagsHint/flagsArgs; flags are stable-sorted high > medium > low. Quirks verified: (1) the grader's 'anaphylaxis AND (pregnant OR immunocompromised)' early-return branch is dead code — it returns exactly what the plain hasAnaphylaxis path returns; (2) the 'draft' short-circuit suppresses rules but NOT flags, which the detector computes independently; (3) VAX-010 (travel rule) fires only when ALL six travel items are null, whereas FLAG-VAX-009 fires only when yellowFever === 0, so the two never fire together; (4) VAX-014 uses consentScore < 50, so an average consent rating of exactly 3 (= 50) is silent; (5) VAX-015 is suppressed when referralNeeded === 'yes' even though FLAG-VAX-010 still fires. Regenerate expected with: bin/test-personas vaccinations-assessment --update",
